# Relative rules only. Workers static assets rejects an absolute URL here
# ("Only relative URLs are allowed"), so the www-to-apex redirect is a
# zone-level Redirect Rule in the dashboard instead. See DEPLOY.md.

# Serve the home page at the bare domain. wrangler's html_handling is set to
# "none" so that /recipes/naan.html is served as itself rather than 307'd to
# /recipes/naan, but turning that off also stops "/" resolving to index.html
# on its own. 200 is a rewrite, not a redirect: the URL stays "/".
/  /index.html  200

# Renamed regions. south-indian.html and himachali.html are still in the
# repository as meta-refresh stubs, which is all GitHub Pages could do; these
# rules mean Cloudflare answers with a real 301 instead, so the ranking follows
# the move rather than leaking. The stub files stay as the fallback if hosting
# ever goes back.
/south-indian.html  /tamil-nadu.html  301
/himachali.html     /pahari.html      301

# The old client-side recipe viewer. Nothing linked to it and every recipe now
# has its own page, but an old bookmark should land somewhere useful.
/recipe.html        /cook.html        301
